.TH QADAM-FLOW-MASTER 1 "October 2026" "Qadam Flow" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qadam-flow-master \- launcher for the Qadam Flow API master process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qadam-flow-master
[\fB\-\-\fR \fInode-arguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qadam-flow-master
starts the Qadam Flow master (API + frontend + scheduler, the \fBapp\fR
container of the Docker image). It is meant to be run by
.BR systemd (1)
as \fBqadam-flow-master.service\fR, not by hand.
.PP
Configuration is read from
.B /etc/qadam-flow/master.conf
(systemd \fIEnvironmentFile\fR). The dashboard is served on
.B AP_PORT
(default 3000) and is normally fronted by a local reverse proxy on 80/443
(recommended \fBnginx\fR), so \fBAP_FRONTEND_URL\fR stays an external
\fBhttps://\fR URL. The master owns the PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector database and
the Redis/Valkey queue; workers connect to it over HTTP
(\fBAP_WORKER_API_URL\fR) and authenticate with a worker token.
.PP
Any extra arguments are passed to
.B node bootstrap.js
after the
.B \-\-
separator.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/qadam-flow/master.conf
Conffile (0600). Secrets are minted automatically on first install and are
never overwritten by upgrades.
.TP
.B /var/lib/qadam-flow/qadam-versions
Qadam version store (run-state data, preserved across upgrades).
.TP
.B /var/cache/qadam-flow
Code-step cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qadam-flow-worker (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Install, distributed-worker and sandboxing notes:
.B /usr/share/doc/qadam-flow-common/README.Debian
and https://flow.aiqadam.org/docs
